{"rule":"The inclination a live launch's closure areas imply, calibrated on the site's own history. history.inclination() reads an inclination from the bearing between the pad and an area's centre (cos i = cos(lat) sin(az)): no Earth rotation, no dog-leg, no curve of the track. Against GCAT that runs off by a few degrees, and by a different amount at each site and on each bearing: the bearing to Xichang's areas for its 35-degree LM-2C and LM-2D launches reads about 31.5, Jiuquan's sun-synchronous launches about 3 high, Taiyuan's about right. A fit of the rotating-earth ground track (live.ground_track) through the areas did no better overall (measured on 24 Nov 2026 over 450 low-orbit launches in the History list with areas and a GCAT inclination: median error -0.5, mean absolute 4.7 degrees, against +1.7 and 4.6 for the bearing; better at Jiuquan, worse at Taiyuan, Mahia and Vandenberg, no help at Xichang): real ascents do not fly a circular orbit from liftoff. So the bearing's reading is corrected by its own error on past launches: of the launches from the same site (within SITE_NM) whose farthest closure area lay within AZ_WIN of this bearing, the K nearest in bearing, MIN_N or more of them, give the median of (reading - GCAT inclination), and that is taken off. Measured leave-one-out on the 519 samples: median error +1.9 -> 0.0, mean absolute 3.5 -> 1.8 degrees, 449 corrected (all within 5 degrees, not the nearest 5: 2.2). Fewer than MIN_N: the bearing's reading stands, and the basis says so. The samples (`samples()`, from the built History list) are low-orbit launches only (LEO, sun-synchronous or polar, space station): a GTO or deep-space payload's inclination is its final orbit's, not the launch's. The bearing is the published path's own (catalog.infer_path): to its farthest closure area, or to the last point of a dog-leg drawn through its areas; a path set by the inclination itself is not a sample. History, not a forecast; an area is never said to be for a launch.","fields":["lon","lat","bearing","inc"],"samples":[[-120.611,34.6327,163.1,73.58],[-120.611,34.6327,186.9,97.67],[-120.611,34.6327,189.4,97.44],[-120.611,34.6327,190.8,97.45],[-120.611,34.6327,191.8,97.66],[-120.611,34.6327,191.8,97.67],[-120.611,34.6327,191.8,97.67],[-120.611,34.6327,191.8,98.4],[-97.1536,25.9964,96.5,26.4],[-97.1536,25.9964,97.9,26.5],[-97.1536,25.9964,99.8,26.5],[-97.1536,25.9964,110.6,26.4],[-97.1536,25.9964,117.0,26.4],[-80.5774,28.5619,88.5,39.99],[-80.5774,28.5619,118.8,43.01],[-80.5774,28.5619,152.2,97.51],[40.5748,62.9278,15.4,82.5],[40.5748,62.9278,15.4,82.5],[40.5748,62.9278,16.3,81.99],[40.5748,62.9278,16.6,82.3],[40.5748,62.9278,16.6,82.3],[40.5748,62.9278,58.7,67.14],[40.5748,62.9278,58.7,67.14],[40.5748,62.9278,340.9,96.46],[40.5748,62.9278,340.9,96.63],[40.5748,62.9278,340.9,96.75],[40.5748,62.9278,340.9,96.76],[40.5748,62.9278,340.9,97.56],[40.5748,62.9278,340.9,97.57],[40.5748,62.9278,340.9,97.88],[40.5748,62.9278,340.9,97.97],[40.5748,62.9278,340.9,98.59],[40.5748,62.9278,342.4,96.59],[40.5748,62.9278,343.5,96.65],[40.5748,62.9278,344.7,96.95],[63.5641,45.996,59.5,51.63],[63.5641,45.996,61.9,51.64],[63.5641,45.996,62.1,51.64],[63.5641,45.996,62.3,51.64],[63.5641,45.996,62.3,51.65],[63.5641,45.996,63.9,51.66],[63.5641,45.996,64.8,51.64],[63.5641,45.996,351.0,96.93],[80.303,13.621,102.5,5.0],[80.303,13.621,102.5,9.66],[80.303,13.621,104.5,9.99],[80.303,13.621,104.5,9.99],[80.303,13.621,136.4,37.2],[80.303,13.621,165.6,87.42],[80.303,13.621,176.9,97.44],[80.303,13.621,177.8,97.56],[100.2908,40.9581,98.0,41.35],[100.2908,40.9581,100.7,41.35],[100.2908,40.9581,100.7,41.47],[100.2908,40.9581,100.7,42.41],[100.2908,40.9581,101.6,41.0],[100.2908,40.9581,102.7,41.46],[100.2908,40.9581,102.7,41.47],[100.2908,40.9581,102.7,41.47],[100.2908,40.9581,102.7,41.47],[100.2908,40.9581,102.7,41.47],[100.2908,40.9581,102.7,41.56],[100.2908,40.9581,102.8,41.47],[100.2908,40.9581,102.8,41.47],[100.2908,40.9581,102.8,41.48],[100.2908,40.9581,104.9